---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalDoc from '../components/LegalDoc.astro';

/**
 * MAINTAINER NOTES
 * - Update `updated` whenever these terms change materially.
 * - No company name, registration number, address or governing law is stated, because
 *   none has been confirmed. Add them here once they exist, ideally after legal review.
 * - This text is a general statement, not legal advice.
 */
const updated = '2026-11-01';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description="The terms for using DEXIRA: website use, intellectual property, editorial content, external links, user submissions, liability and changes."
>
  <LegalDoc
    title="Terms and Conditions"
    intro="These terms describe how you may use the DEXIRA website. Please read them before using it."
    updated={updated}
  >
    <h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance of terms</h2>
    <p>
      By accessing or using DEXIRA, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with them,
      please do not use the website.
    </p>

    <h2 id="use">Website use</h2>
    <p>You may use DEXIRA for lawful, personal and informational purposes. You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>interfere with the operation or security of the website;</li>
      <li>attempt to gain unauthorised access to the website or its systems;</li>
      <li>use automated tools to copy the site at a scale that harms its performance;</li>
      <li>use the website in a way that breaks the law or the rights of others.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="intellectual-property">Intellectual property and copyright</h2>
    <p>
      The content on DEXIRA, including text, design, logos and illustrations, belongs to DEXIRA
      or is used with permission, and is protected by copyright and other laws. You may read it,
      share links to it, and quote short extracts with clear credit and a link back to the
      original story. You may not copy, republish, sell or distribute substantial parts of the
      content without our written permission.
    </p>

    <h2 id="editorial">Editorial content and informational purposes</h2>
    <p>
      Our stories are published for general information and discussion. They are not professional
      advice of any kind, including legal, financial, medical, security or business advice.
      Before acting on anything you read here, consider seeking advice from a qualified
      professional. We aim to be accurate and to correct mistakes, but we cannot guarantee that
      every story is complete or current. Some content on the site may be sample material used
      while the publication is being developed.
    </p>

    <h2 id="external-links">External links</h2>
    <p>
      DEXIRA may link to websites and services run by others. We include links for convenience
      and do not control or endorse those sites. We are not responsible for their content or
      practices, and your use of them is at your own risk.
    </p>

    <h2 id="submissions">User submissions</h2>
    <p>
      You may send us messages, feedback, corrections and story suggestions. By doing so you
      confirm that what you send is yours to share and does not break the law or anyone else's
      rights. You allow us to use your feedback and suggestions to improve DEXIRA, without
      obligation to you. We are not obliged to reply to or publish anything you send. How we
      handle personal information in submissions is described in the
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      DEXIRA is provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo; basis. To the
      fullest extent permitted by law, DEXIRA is not liable for any loss or damage arising from
      your use of, or inability to use, the website or from reliance on its content. Nothing in
      these terms limits any liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of the page shows when
      they were last updated. Continuing to use DEXIRA after a change means you accept the
      updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact information</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms are welcome. Please use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="about-terms">About this document</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are a general statement and are not legal advice.
    </p>
  </LegalDoc>
</Layout>
